{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d078ef6781167ad064cf6da48c6ae0fd56b267b5736efac0fe48bbacc8a874ab","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconcile Bridge observability & CloudWatch integration","key_entities":[".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","rebar/host:bridge_run_failures","aws_iam_role.gha_bridge_metrics","aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.bridge_run_failures","infra/terraform/iam_bridge_metrics.tf","infra/terraform/monitoring_bridge.tf","aws_iam_openid_connect_provider.github","cloudwatch:PutMetricData","cloudwatch:namespace"],"problem_keywords":["cloudwatch observability","github actions monitoring","bridge run failures","metric publishing","alarm detection","oidc authentication"],"propositions":["Reconcile Bridge run failures on GitHub Actions produced no CloudWatch signal, leaving outages invisible to monitoring until operator manually inspects workflow run details.","Bridge failure metric must publish a value (1 on failure, 0 on success) to distinguish a healthy-but-absent publisher from a broken publisher, keeping the alarm in OK state rather than INSUFFICIENT_DATA during normal operation.","A narrowly-scoped IAM role must grant only cloudwatch:PutMetricData permission constrained by cloudwatch:namespace=rebar/host condition, using existing OIDC federation to avoid widening drift-detection or existing roles.","CloudWatch alarm on bridge_run_failures must use period=3600 with threshold=1 to page on sustained failures (second failure within an hour) while tolerating routine transient blips from single failed runs."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":178789